--TEST--
Core\Imap::open checks `imap.connect` for the block's name before it reads any configuration, so an ungranted name throws `RuntimeError` and does not show which blocks exist — `rule:core-classes/imap`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `imap.connect` grants `inbox` and nothing else. `archive` is a block in `nvs.toml`,
// but it is not granted, so `open` throws.
try {
    var $archive = Core\Imap::open("archive");
    echo "opened archive", "\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $refused) {
    echo $refused->message, "\n";
}

// A name with no block throws the same error.
try {
    var $nothing = Core\Imap::open("nothing");
    echo "opened nothing", "\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $refused) {
    echo $refused->message, "\n";
}

// The error can be caught, and the program keeps running.
echo "still running", "\n";
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.imap]
connect = ["inbox"]

[imap.inbox]
host = "127.0.0.1"
port = 1
user = "ada@example.com"
password = "secret"

[imap.archive]
host = "127.0.0.1"
port = 1
user = "ada@example.com"
password = "secret"
--EXPECT--
Core\Imap::open needs the capability `imap.connect` for archive, which is not granted
help: add `connect = ["archive"]` under `[capabilities.imap]` in nvs.toml
Core\Imap::open needs the capability `imap.connect` for nothing, which is not granted
help: add `connect = ["nothing"]` under `[capabilities.imap]` in nvs.toml
still running
